{"name":"Moonlit Orchid","hex":"#949194","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"moonlit","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Lit by moonlight."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/moonlit"},{"term":"orchid","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A plant of the orchid family (Orchidaceae), bearing unusually-shaped flowers of beautiful colours. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","A light bluish-red, violet-red or purple colour."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a light purple colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/orchid"}],"entries":[{"title":"Moonlight","blocks":[{"text":"Moonlight is light from the surface of the Moon, consisting mostly of reflected sunlight, and some earthlight."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dc/Earthshine_Moon.jpg/330px-Earthshine_Moon.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Moonlight","wikidata":"Q1058800"},{"title":"Orchid","blocks":[{"text":"Orchids are plants that belong to the family Orchidaceae, a diverse and widespread group of flowering plants with blooms that are often colourful and fragrant. Orchids are cosmopolitan plants, living in diverse habitats on every continent except Antarctica. The world's richest diversity of orchid genera and species is in the tropics. Many species are epiphytes, living on trees. The flowers and their pollination mechanisms are highly specialized, attracting insect pollinators by colour, pattern, scent, pheromones, and sometimes by mimicking female insects. Orchids have very small seeds, relying on fungal partners for germination. Some orchids have no leaves, either photosynthesizing with their roots or relying entirely on fungal partners for food."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Plant_Orchid_Cymbidium_aloifolium_P1110661_05_-_cropped.jpg/330px-Plant_Orchid_Cymbidium_aloif